# DDD Architecture — Place Module

## Layer Responsibilities

### Domain (src/modules/place/domain/)
The pure core — zero framework dependencies, zero imports from outer layers.

- `aggregates/` — Aggregate roots enforce business invariants. All mutations go through the root.
- `value-objects/` — Immutable, self-validating objects (no setters, throw on invalid input).
- `events/` — Plain data objects describing something that happened inside the domain.

**Rules:**
- Domain MUST NOT import from `application/` or `infrastructure/`.
- Aggregates MUST validate all state transitions internally.
- Value objects MUST be immutable (use `readonly` on all fields).
- Domain events MUST be named in past tense: `PlaceCreatedEvent`, `ReviewAddedEvent`.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — value object is immutable and self-validates
export class Location {
  constructor(
    readonly lat: number,
    readonly lng: number,
  ) {
    if (lat < -90 || lat > 90) throw new Error('Invalid latitude');
    if (lng < -180 || lng > 180) throw new Error('Invalid longitude');
  }
}

// ❌ BAD — mutable, no validation
export class Location {
  lat: number;
  lng: number;
}
```

---

### Application (src/modules/place/application/)
Orchestrates use cases — no business logic, only coordination.

- `commands/` — Write side (CQRS). Use case files named `<verb>-<noun>.use-case.ts`.
- `queries/` — Read side (CQRS). Handler files named `<verb>-<noun>.handler.ts`. MAY bypass domain.
- `ports/` — Interfaces (contracts) the application depends on. Named `<noun>.port.ts`.

**Rules:**
- Commands MUST load aggregate via port → mutate → persist via port → emit events.
- Queries MUST NOT load domain aggregates — read directly from the read-model repository port.
- Application MUST NOT import from `infrastructure/` directly — only via port interfaces.
- A use case MUST do exactly one thing. Split if multiple responsibilities emerge.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — command use case pattern
export class CreatePlaceUseCase {
  constructor(private readonly placeRepo: PlaceRepositoryPort) {}

  async execute(cmd: CreatePlaceCommand): Promise<void> {
    const place = Place.create(cmd);   // domain logic inside aggregate
    await this.placeRepo.save(place);
  }
}

// ❌ BAD — business logic leaking into application layer
async execute(cmd: CreatePlaceCommand): Promise<void> {
  if (cmd.name.length < 3) throw new Error('Too short'); // belongs in domain
  await this.placeRepo.save(cmd);
}
```

---

### Presentation (src/modules/place/presentation/)
HTTP entrypoints for the module.

- Controllers translate HTTP request/response to application commands and queries.

### Infrastructure (src/modules/place/infrastructure/)
External implementations that satisfy output ports.

- `driven-adapters/` — Repository implementations. Implement ports defined in `application/ports/`.

**Rules:**
- Controllers MUST NOT contain business logic — delegate entirely to use cases / query handlers.
- Repository implementations MUST implement the corresponding port interface.
- Naming: `postgres-<noun>.repository.ts`, `postgis-<noun>.repository.ts`, `<noun>.controller.ts`.
- Write repositories use PostgreSQL; read repositories use PostGIS for spatial queries.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — thin controller
export class CatalogController {
  constructor(private readonly searchNearest: SearchNearestHandler) {}

  async search(req: Request, res: Response) {
    const result = await this.searchNearest.handle(req.query);
    res.json(result);
  }
}

// ❌ BAD — controller doing DB work
async search(req: Request, res: Response) {
  const places = await db.query('SELECT * FROM places WHERE ...');
  res.json(places);
}
```

---

## Dependency Direction (strictly enforced)

```
presentation → application → domain
infrastructure → application → domain
```

**Never allow:**
- `domain` importing from `application` or `infrastructure`
- `application` importing from `infrastructure`
- `application` importing from `presentation`
- Cross-module imports without going through a published port

---

## File Naming Convention

| Layer | Pattern | Example |
|-------|---------|---------|
| Aggregate root | `<noun>.root.ts` | `place.root.ts` |
| Value object | `<noun>.vo.ts` | `location.vo.ts` |
| Domain event | `<noun>.event.ts` | `place-created.event.ts` |
| Command use case | `<verb>-<noun>.use-case.ts` | `create-place.use-case.ts` |
| Query handler | `<verb>-<noun>.handler.ts` | `search-nearest.handler.ts` |
| Port interface | `<noun>.port.ts` | `place-repository.port.ts` |
| Repository impl | `<db>-<noun>.repository.ts` | `postgres-place.repository.ts` |
| Controller | `<context>.controller.ts` | `catalog.controller.ts` |
